innovations.desc:
Volunteers and service users are invited to identify five essential personal skills required to take control of one’s own life and play an active role in society:
Persuading without manipulating: knowing how to present arguments, defend a point of view and listen to the person you are speaking to;
Finding information and avoiding misinformation: knowing how to use internet search engines, identify different sources of information, cross-check sources and verify their relevance;
Nurturing and enriching one’s social environment: building and strengthening one’s network, staying connected to avoid isolation;
Understanding how the modern world works: key issues and power dynamics, the economy, politics, globalisation and citizenship;
Developing self-confidence and self-awareness.
