As part of an “outreach” approach based on collaboration and partnership with various local stakeholders (social housing providers, cultural and sociocultural institutions, schools, nonprofit organizations, citizen councils, residents, and public authorities), PaQ’la Lune carries out “art projects” in about a dozen priority neighborhoods (QPVs), particularly on the streets or at the base of apartment buildings. There, it offers various activities for exploring and practicing the arts, as well as outreach tools that contribute to the realization of cultural rights, with a particular focus on youth.
PaQ’la Lune’s activities are divided into three areas: cultural and social events, artistic practice activities, and artistic creations. The program is developed collectively.
Cultural and social events:
street and building-front events;
discussion cafés, social gatherings, picnics;
