The first edition of the program has just concluded and is still undergoing a thorough evaluation regarding the results achieved. Among the main outputs, the following can be highlighted:
8 start-ups supported;
7 sprints (comprising planning sessions and demo-days);
7 thematic workshops;
50+ hours of one-to-one mentoring;
€48,000 in grants awarded.
The program also included a research study conducted by EURICSE, which resulted in the report “ Youth, Activism, and the Social Economy in Tuscany: Trends, Challenges, and Contrasts ”, available here: https://euricse.eu/it/publications/25002-2/

COEXIST strengthens local communities’ ability to support the social inclusion of Ukrainian refugees through innovation, mentoring, and cross-sector collaboration. The project develops evidence-based methodologies led by the University of Wroclaw, enhancing the quality and effectiveness of inclusion practices. Among its main results are:
creation of a research-informed model for community-driven refugee inclusion;
training of local mentors to guide integration processes;
establishment of collaborative networks between NGOs, local authorities, and educational institutions;
increased awareness…

innovations.desc:
The programme is based on weekly 1.5-hour workshops via videoconference, supervised by qualified neuropsychologists. These intensive sessions, much like physical exercise, provide real benefits in terms of cognitive functioning, quality of life, and social impact.
Specialist professionals focus on several key areas to help restore cognitive abilities :
Therapeutic education for patients;
Psycho-education and metacognition;
Learning cognitive strategies to adapt to new capacities;
Intensified individual work within multi-level groups.

To support young people´s independence and law-abiding behavior, we provide them a mentor, as well, as access to a half-way house. These opportunities are mainly focused on those who are being released from prison or whose sentence has been suspended, as but also those who are:
In custody or have recently been released,
On probation;
Accused or being investigated in pre-trial proceedings;
Assigned alternative sentence instead of imprisonment or measures suitable for minors or young adults;
In a closed juvenile institution or have just excited one;
Repeatedly committing minor offenses and assigned corrective measures or obligations.
The role of mentor is to guide and assist youngsters in rebuilding their lives and managing daily challenges, ultimately reducing the risk of reoffending. If a young person is serving a prison sentence, the mentor will start meeting with them up to six months…

INNOVCare’s specific objectives included:
Assessing the unmet social needs of people with rare diseases and their family members, often the main carers;
Implementing a pilot in Romania;
Analysing its socioeconomic impact and the cost-benefit;
Promoting the exchange of good practices via multi-stakeholder workshops and the creation of an European Network of Resource Centres for Rare Diseases;
Analysing opportunities/challenges to upscale the care model to other MS and beyond RD;
Strengthening partnerships between public, private and civil society organisations.

